# Build context trim for `docker build -f docker/Dockerfile .` (root context, whole reactor).
#
# docker/Dockerfile deliberately does `COPY . .` rather than listing modules: the reactor builds
# `service`'s dependency on `qits-cd-domain` from source (it is never published), and a module list
# would have to be edited every time a module is added. This file is what makes that cheap — it
# drops everything the build does not need, so no stale output leaks in.

.git
.gitignore

# Maven / Quarkus build output — regenerated inside the build stage, and it is the bulk of a working
# tree here. Copying it in would also risk a stale target/ shadowing what the stage compiles.
**/target
**/target-ide

# The webui submodule's install output: a symlink farm full of platform-native binaries compiled for
# the host rather than for ubi9, and nothing in the build stage reads it — the stage runs no install
# and no client build (see docker/Dockerfile). `.angular` is the CLI's own cache, the same shape of
# host-local junk.
#
# NOTE THE ASYMMETRY with the platform's Quinoa recipe
# (docs/project-setup-quinoa-angular.md in the qits superproject), which excludes the client's dist/
# as well: here dist/ is the PAYLOAD. qits-spa-cd depends on @qits/ui-components, which exists only
# on the platform's own npm registry, reachable from no address a docker build has — so the bundle
# is built BEFORE this image by .config/qits/ci-post-receive.yml, on qits-net where that registry
# answers. Excluding dist/ would fail the build at the `test -f` guard on the mvnw line. Every
# SPA-serving service in the platform carries this same departure, for the same reason.
**/node_modules
service/src/main/webui/.angular

# Local env / IDE cruft
.env
.idea
.vscode
.sdkmanrc

# Docs and the docker/ dir itself: nothing in the build reads them, and keeping them out means
# editing this Dockerfile or a README does not bust the `COPY . .` layer.
*.md
docs
docker
